    "pressure": {
      "file": "vibration_monitoring_system_pressure.glb",
      "title": "Severity zones guide action",
      "description": "Casing vibration (velocity, mm/s RMS, 10–1000 Hz) is judged against ISO 20816 zones A (new) → B (unrestricted) → C (limited time) → D (damage likely); shaft displacement from proximity probes (µm pk-pk) is used on oil-film bearing machines. Trends and spectra reveal causes: 1× running speed — unbalance; 2× and axial — misalignment; bearing defect frequencies (BPFO / BPFI) — rolling bearing damage; sub-synchronous — oil whirl. The rack raises alerts and trips per API 670 logic (voting, delays).",
      "render": "normal",
      "annotations": []
